menu "Motor Controller Configuration"

    config MOTOR_CTRL_DEFAULT_COUNTS_PER_REV
        int "Default encoder counts per output revolution"
        default 1440
        range 1 1000000
        help
            Total encoder quadrature counts per one full revolution of the shaft
            being measured. For a 4x-decoded quadrature encoder with N pulses/rev,
            set this to N * 4. Example: a 360 CPR encoder gives 1440 counts/rev.
            Overridden per-instance via MotorControllerConfig::counts_per_rev.

    config MOTOR_CTRL_DEFAULT_VEL_FILTER_CUTOFF_HZ
        int "Default velocity estimate filter cutoff (Hz)"
        default 50
        range 0 10000
        help
            Cutoff frequency of the first-order low-pass filter applied to the
            velocity estimate. Velocity is computed every update() from the
            encoder count delta divided by dt, which is coarsely quantized at
            high loop rates (one count per period), so some filtering is
            usually needed. Lower cutoffs give smoother readings but add phase
            lag to the velocity loop. 0 disables the filter.
            Overridden per-instance via
            MotorControllerConfig::velocity_filter_cutoff_hz.

endmenu
